e. Medmenham, UK.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-ehp0114s1-000106"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Au</surname><given-names>DWT</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>The application of histocytopathological biomarkers in marine pollution monitoring: a review</article-title><source>Mar Poll Bull</source><volume>48</volume><fpage>817</fpage><lpage>834</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b11-ehp0114s1-000106"><mixed-citation publication-type="other">Battelle. 2003. Comparative Evaluation of Vitellogenin Methods for Medaka and Zebrafish. Draft Final Report for U.S EPA Work Assignment 2-26, July 2003. Washington, DC:U.S. Environmental Protection Agency.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-ehp0114s1-000106"><mixed-citation publication-type="other">Battelle. 2005. Multi-chemical Evaluation of the Short&#x02013;Term Reproduction Assay with the Fathead Minnow. Contract Report 68-W-01-023, Work Assignment 5-5, Task 7. Washington, DC:Office of Prevention, Pesticides, and Toxic Substances, U.S. Environmental Protection Agency.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-ehp0114s1-000106"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Westerlund</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Olsson</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Regulation of Arctic char (<italic>Salvelinus alpinus</italic>) egg shell proteins and vitellogenin during reproduction and in response to 17[beta]-estradiol and cortisol</article-title><source>Gen Comp Endocrinol</source><volume>135</volume><fpage>276</fpage><lpage>285</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14723879</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b14-ehp0114s1-000106"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Bigsby</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Chapin</sur